
Setup & Build

| Command                           | Description                                                                   |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose up`               | Builds, (re)creates, starts containers in the background (if not using `-d`). |
| `docker-compose up -d`            | Same as above, but runs in detached mode (in the background).                 |
| `docker-compose build`            | Builds the images defined in your `docker-compose.yml`.                       |
| `docker-compose build --no-cache` | Rebuilds images without using cache.                                          |


 Stop & Remove

| Command               | Description                                                      |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose down` | Stops and removes all containers, networks, and volumes defined. |
| `docker-compose stop` | Stops the running containers without removing them.              |
| `docker-compose rm`   | Removes stopped containers.                                      |


Info & Debugging

| Command                  | Description                                                     |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose ps`      | Lists the status of all containers defined in the Compose file. |
| `docker-compose logs`    | Shows logs for all services.                                    |
| `docker-compose logs -f` | Follows logs in real time (like `tail -f`).                     |
| `docker-compose top`     | Displays running processes in the containers.                   |


Exec & Run Commands Inside Containers

| Command                                   | Description                                                                            |
| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose exec <service> <command>` | Runs a command in a running container (e.g., `docker-compose exec homefinance bash`).  |
| `docker-compose run <service> <command>`  | Runs a one-off command in a new container (e.g., `docker-compose run homefinance sh`). |


Volumes & Cleanup

| Command                     | Description                                                   |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose down -v`    | Removes containers and **named volumes** defined in the file. |
| `docker volume ls`          | List Docker volumes.                                          |
| `docker volume rm <volume>` | Remove a specific volume.                                     |



Restart

| Command                            | Description                  |
| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `docker-compose restart`           | Restarts all the containers. |
| `docker-compose restart <service>` | Restart a specific service.  |


Using Specific Compose Files or Projects

| Command                                   | Description                                              |
| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose -f custom-compose.yml up` | Use a specific Compose file.                             |
| `docker-compose -p myproject up`          | Set a custom project name instead of the directory name. |

